[40.74, "o", "The best fit is the **Google BigQuery Managed MCP Server** (`urn:ai:google.com:mcp:bigquery`), which can execute SQL queries, inspect schemas, and do dry-run cost estimation on live BigQuery data.\r\n\r\nIt's Tier 3 (requires GCP auth). No GCP credentials are currently active. To proceed, you'd run on your terminal:\r\n```\r\ngcloud auth application-default login\r\n```\r\n\r\nWant me to enable BigQuery and have you run that auth command? (Note the free tier covers 1TB of query processing/month.)\r\n"]
[43.24, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[43.24, "o", "developer@workstation:~/ard-project$ "]
