[90.275, "o", "\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"Onboard and authenticate to Google Cloud services using Application Default Credentials and gcloud\"}\r\n"]
[92.775, "o", "\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_record_decision {\"decision\":\"allowed\",\"service_identifier\":\"urn:ai:google.com:mcp:gcloud\"}\r\n"]
[95.275, "o", "Your gcloud CLI is installed but no credentials are active. Please run these on your terminal to log in:\r\n\r\n```\r\ngcloud auth application-default login\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis opens a browser to grant the Application Default Credentials (ADC) used by Google MCP servers (Cloud Run, gcloud Resource Manager, etc.). If you also want regular gcloud access:\r\n\r\n```\r\ngcloud auth login\r\ngcloud config set project YOUR_PROJECT_ID\r\n```\r\n\r\nBoth are free-tier friendly (no charges for auth). Let me know when done and I'll verify.\r\n"]
[97.614, "o", "\u001b[?2004hdeveloper@workstation:~/ard-project$ "]
