[167.382, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[167.554, "o", "================================================================================\r\n\ud83d\ude80 RUNNING OPENCODE CONTAINERIZED ARD E2E TEST SUITE\r\n================================================================================\r\n\r\n================================================================================\r\n"]
[167.554, "o", "\ud83e\uddea SCENARIO 1: Pure Public Discovery (Tier 0 Zero-Auth Counterpoint)"]
[167.554, "o", "\r\n================================================================================\r\n"]
[170.054, "o", "I'll search for tools that can help with SQL query optimization and zero-trust security design.\r\nFound matching tools \u2014 all free, no auth needed:\r\n\r\n**SQL optimization:**\r\n- **BigQuery SQL & Performance Guidelines** \u2014 query optimization, partitioning/clustering, schema design, window functions\r\n- **Cloud SQL/AlloyDB/Spanner Database Design** \u2014 normalization, indexing, connection pooling, migrations\r\n- **Well-Architected Performance Efficiency** \u2014 caching, read replicas, load testing (bonus)\r\n\r\n**Zero-trust security:**\r\n- **Well-Architected Security** \u2014 zero-trust patterns, IAM least-privilege, network perimeters, encryption\r\n\r\nFor live querying against real data, `bigquery.mcp.google.com` could help, but it needs `gcloud auth application-default login`. Want me to load the BigQuery and Security skills for detailed offline guidance?\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"SQL query optimization best practices and performance tuning\"}\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"zero-trust security architecture design best practices\"}\r\n\r\n\u2705 Scenario 1 Passed: OpenCode returned Tier 0 skills with zero auth friction.\r\n\r\n================================================================================\r\n\ud83e\uddea SCENARIO 2: Cloud Intent -> User Opts Out ('No with an opt out')\r\n================================================================================\r\n"]
[172.554, "o", "--- Turn 1 (Agent Response) ---\r\nThe **Google BigQuery Managed MCP Server** (`urn:ai:google.com:mcp:bigquery`) is the tool \u2014 it executes live SQL, inspects schemas, and estimates query costs, and handles 100GB datasets easily.\r\n\r\nIt requires GCP credentials (Tier 3). Would you like to onboard? If so, I'll record your decision and give you the auth command.\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"run live analytical SQL query on large sales dataset in BigQuery\"}\r\n\r\n"]
[175.054, "o", "--- Turn 2 (Opt-Out Response) ---\r\nGCP discovery is now opted out. I'll skip Google Cloud services in future search results.\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_set_preference {\"mode\":\"opt_out\"}\r\n\r\n\u2705 Scenario 2 Passed: OpenCode asked to log into GCP, user opted out, and GCP was silenced.\r\n\r\n================================================================================\r\n\ud83e\uddea SCENARIO 3: Cloud Intent -> User Onboards ('Yes') -> Human OAuth & Live BigQuery Query\r\n================================================================================\r\n"]
[177.554, "o", "--- Turn 1 (Agent Response) ---\r\nThe **Google BigQuery Managed MCP Server** (`urn:ai:google.com:mcp:bigquery`) does this \u2014 it executes SQL queries, inspects table schemas, and explores public datasets.\r\n\r\nLet me check your auth status since it requires\r\nThe tool that can query public BigQuery datasets is the **Google BigQuery Managed MCP Server** (`urn:ai:google.com:mcp:bigquery`). It supports SQL execution, schema inspection, and public-dataset exploration, but requires GCP auth (Tier 3) \u2014 your environment currently has no active credentials.\r\n\r\nWould you like me to persist consent to onboard this service so I can set up auth? If so, you'd run `gcloud auth application-default login` on your terminal.\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"query public BigQuery dataset SQL\"}\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_auth_status Unknown\r\n\r\n"]
[180.054, "o", "--- Turn 2 (Onboarding Instructions) ---\r\nTo log in, run this in your terminal:\r\n\r\n```\r\ngcloud auth application-default login\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis opens a browser to authenticate and stores ADC credentials (`gcloud` is already installed). After it completes, let me know and I'll verify your auth status.\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_auth_status Unknown\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_record_decision {\"service_identifier\":\"urn:ai:google.com:mcp:gcp\",\"decision\":\"onboarded\"}\r\n\r\n--- Turn 3 (Human OAuth Flow) ---\r\n"]
[181.78, "o", "Go to the following link in your browser, and complete the sign-in prompts:\r\n\r\n    https://accounts.google.com/o/oauth2/auth?response_type=code&client_id=[REDACTED_CLIENT_ID]...&redirect_uri=https%3A%2F%2Fsdk.cloud.google.com%2Fapplicationdefaultauthcode.html&scope=openid+https%3A%2F%2Fwww.googleapis.com%2Fauth%2Fuserinfo.email+https%3A%2F%2Fwww.googleapis.com%2Fauth%2Fcloud-platform&state=[REDACTED]&prompt=consent&access_type=offline\r\n\r\nEnter verification code: 4/0AXEQxID[REDACTED_OAUTH_CODE]\r\n\r\nCredentials saved to file: [/workspace/.config/gcloud/application_default_credentials.json]\r\n\r\nThese credentials will be used by any library that requests Application Default Credentials (ADC).\r\nQuota project \"alanblount-sandbox\" was added to ADC which can be used by Google client libraries for billing and quota.\r\n\r\n"]
[184.28, "o", "--- Turn 4 (Post-Auth Live Query Response) ---\r\nThis query requires the **BigQuery MCP server** (`urn:ai:google.com:mcp:bigquery`), which is a Tier 3 service needing GCP Application Default Credentials. Your environment is currently **unauthenticated** (no service account or user ADC detected).\r\n\r\nTo proceed, I need your consent to use the BigQuery MCP server. It also requires you to authenticate on your machine:\r\n\r\n1. Do you consent to using the BigQuery MCP server to run this query?\r\n2. If yes, run this in your terminal and then let me know:\r\n\r\n```\r\ngcloud auth application-default login\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe BigQuery free tier (1TB/month of query processing) covers this query, so there's no cost. Once authenticated, I'll run the query against `bigquery-public-data.usa_names.usa_1910_current`.\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_auth_status Unknown\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"Run SQL queries against Google BigQuery public datasets\"}\r\n\r\n"]
[184.281, "o", "Traceback (most recent call last):\r\n"]
[184.282, "o", "  File \u001b[35m\"/usr/local/google/home/alanblount/Workspaces/open-source/ard-plugin-exploration/tests/e2e_podman_runner.py\"\u001b[0m, line \u001b[35m233\u001b[0m, in \u001b[35m<module>\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[31mrun_all_e2e_tests\u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m()\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[31m~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m^^\u001b[0m\r\n  File \u001b[35m\"/usr/local/google/home/alanblount/Workspaces/open-source/ard-plugin-exploration/tests/e2e_podman_runner.py\"\u001b[0m, line \u001b[35m224\u001b[0m, in \u001b[35mrun_all_e2e_tests\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[31mtest_3_scenario_3_onboarding_flow\u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m()\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[31m~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m^^\u001b[0m\r\n  File \u001b[35m\"/usr/local/google/home/alanblount/Workspaces/open-source/ard-plugin-exploration/tests/e2e_podman_runner.py\"\u001b[0m, line \u001b[35m184\u001b[0m, in \u001b[35mtest_3_scenario_3_onboarding_flow\u001b[0m\r\n    \"liam\" in out4.lower()\r\n    ...<3 lines>...\r\n    or \"19777\" in out4\r\n\u001b[1;35mAssertionError\u001b[0m: \u001b[35mTurn 4 did not return real BigQuery results\u001b[0m\r\n"]
